tcpecho: line echo over 127.0.0.1, port 0
server A: stops after 4 connections
ok echo: lines come back byte-for-byte
ok partial: no reply while the line is open
ok partial: reply once the line completes
ok idle: ERR idle timeout, then the server closes
ok long line: 100 bytes get ERR line too long, then a close
server A log:
  conn 1: closed by client
  conn 2: closed by client
  conn 3: idle timeout
  conn 4: line too long
ok server A stopped after 4 connections
server B: stops on QUIT
ok again: echo
ok QUIT: BYE, then the server closes
server B log:
  conn 1: closed by client
  conn 2: QUIT
ok server B stopped on QUIT
ok after QUIT: a new connection is refused
failures: 0
